# React patterns

- Prefer Server Components. Add `'use client'` only for interactivity, browser APIs, or client-only hooks.
- Colocate UI: `ComponentName/ComponentName.tsx` + optional `ComponentName.module.css` + `index.ts` re-export.
- Tailwind for one-off layout/spacing; CSS Modules for component-specific styles; tokens in `@/shared/styles/tokens.css`.
- Pass Server Component output as `children` into client shells (e.g. `HeaderMenu` → `HeaderContainer`) instead of fetching on the client.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — client fetch just to render static nav
'use client';
useEffect(() => { void loadMenu().then(setMenu); }, []);

// ✅ GOOD — server load, client only where needed
export async function HeaderMenu() {
  const menu = await getMenu();
  return <nav>...</nav>;
}
```
